    "track": "dsa",
    "id": "topological",
    "title": "Topological order & dependency graphs",
    "level": "Core",
    "minutes": 20,
    "summary": "Order work by prerequisites and detect impossible dependency cycles.",
    "concepts": [
      [
        "Orient the edge carefully",
        "Use prerequisite → dependent. The indegree of a vertex is the number of unfinished prerequisites. Vertices with indegree zero are ready."
      ],
      [
        "Kahn’s algorithm removes ready work",
        "Place all zero-indegree vertices in a queue. Remove one, append it to the order, and decrement the indegree of its dependents. A dependent becomes ready exactly when its indegree reaches zero."
      ],
      [
        "A cycle leaves unfinished work",
        "If fewer than V vertices are processed, the graph has a directed cycle. There can be multiple valid topological orders. Use a priority queue if the smallest available label must come first."
      ]
    ],
    "example": "With A → C, B → C, C → D, either A,B,C,D or B,A,C,D is valid. Adding D → A creates a cycle A → C → D → A. B can be removed, but the remaining cycle never becomes ready.",
    "code": "#include <optional>\n#include <queue>\n#include <utility>\n#include <vector>\nstd::optional<std::vector<int>> topoOrder(\n    int n, const std::vector<std::pair<int,int>>& edges) {\n    std::vector<std::vector<int>> graph(n);\n    std::vector<int> indegree(n), order;\n    for (auto [u,v] : edges) { graph[u].push_back(v); ++indegree[v]; }\n    std::queue<int> ready;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) if (indegree[i] == 0) ready.push(i);\n    while (!ready.empty()) {\n        int u = ready.front(); ready.pop(); order.push_back(u);\n        for (int v : graph[u]) if (--indegree[v] == 0) ready.push(v);\n    }\n    if (static_cast<int>(order.size()) != n) return std::nullopt;\n    return order;\n} // Require n >= 0 and vertex IDs in [0,n).",
